an facing multiple felony charges, including sexual misconduct with a minor and...","language":"en","text":"𝗠𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗶𝗻 𝗖𝗼𝘂𝗻𝘁𝘆; 𝗠𝗮𝗻 𝗘𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿𝘀 𝗚𝘂𝗶𝗹𝘁𝘆 𝗣𝗹𝗲𝗮 𝗶𝗻 𝗖𝗵𝗶𝗹𝗱 𝗦𝗲𝘅𝘂𝗮𝗹 𝗠𝗶𝘀𝗰𝗼𝗻𝗱𝘂𝗰𝘁 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗞𝗶𝗱𝗻𝗮𝗽𝗽𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗖𝗮𝘀𝗲\n\nSHOALS, Ind. — A 29-year-old man facing multiple felony charges, including sexual misconduct with a minor and kidnapping, has entered a guilty plea in Martin Circuit Court, resulting in the cancellation of his upcoming jury trial.\n\nAccording to Indiana MyCase court records, Timothy S. Morrow Jr. entered a guilty plea that was accepted by the court on October 26, 2026. Judicial Officer Isha E. Wright-Ryan signed an order accepting the plea and directed that a presentence investigation be completed.\n\nMorrow was booked into custody on October 27, 2026, at approximately 2:53 p.m.\n\nThe case, filed March 9, 2026, includes three felony counts stemming from alleged incidents in 2024 and 2026.\n\nCourt records list the alleged offense date for the sexual misconduct and kidnapping charges as February 1, 2024. The intimidation charge stems from an alleged incident on January 16, 2026.\n\nThe kidnapping charge alleges the offense involved the use of a vehicle, while the intimidation charge alleges a threat to commit a forcible felony.\n\nFollowing the court's acceptance of the guilty plea, a three-day jury trial scheduled for November 17-19, 2026, was canceled.\n\nA presentence investigation will allow the court to gather information before determining sentencing.\n\nCharges:\n\n- Sexual Misconduct With a Minor — Level 4 Felony\n\nIndiana Code 35-42-4-9(a)\n\n- Kidnapping — Level 5 Felony\n\nIndiana Code 35-42-3-2(a)\n\n- Intimidation — Level 6 Felony\n\nIndiana Code 35-45-2-1(a)(4)\n\nThe case remains pending sentencing. Any sentence will be determined by the court.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n14 comments\n\n9 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\n3\n\nMost relevant is selected, so some comments may have been filtered out.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":3333.3890330104623,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}